      "content": "I assess that shifting from live predictive modeling to manual, offline analysis will introduce latency risks, as manual analysis typically takes 1-2 days to produce comparable results. This delay will affect the timeliness of response interventions, potentially prolonging patient care days and increasing the risk of hospitalization. Moreover, manual modeling will lack the scalability and reliability of live instance predictive outputs, which could impact the overall effectiveness of pandemic response efforts.",
      "source": "target",
